        417.31878662109375,
        374.56390380859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CMDP Approaches",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        382.04534912109375,
        186.3060302734375,
        390.951904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Proximal Policy Optimization-Lagrangian. PPOLag is a primal-dual method using Proximal Policy",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        399.414794921875,
        504.3514709472656,
        408.44091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Optimization [33] based off of the implementation found in [7]. The lagrange multiplier is a scalar",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        410.443359375,
        504.1732482910156,
        419.34991455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "learnable parameter.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        421.35235595703125,
        188.7767791748047,
        430.2589111328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Constraint-Rectified Policy Optimization. CRPO [35] is a primal approach that switches between",
      "bbox": [
        107.6709976196289,
        437.6217956542969,
        503.9978942871094,
        446.6479187011719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "optimizing for rewards and minimizing constraint violations depending on whether the constraints",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        448.6503601074219,
        504.0042724609375,
        457.5569152832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "are violated.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        459.5593566894531,
        157.24513244628906,
        468.4659118652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Penalized Proximal Policy Optimization. P3O [32] is another primal approach based on applying the",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        475.82879638671875,
        504.00311279296875,
        484.85491943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "technique of clipping the surrogate objectives found in PPO [33] to CMDPs.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        486.85736083984375,
        412.4968566894531,
        495.763916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Projection-Based Constrained Policy Optimization. PCPO [3] is a trust-region approach that takes",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        503.12579345703125,
        504.0022277832031,
        512.1519165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a step in policy parameter space toward optimizing for reward and then projects this policy to the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        514.1543579101562,
        503.99737548828125,
        523.0609130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constraint set satisfying the CMDP expected cost constraints.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        525.0643310546875,
        351.9143371582031,
        533.9708862304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hard Constraints Approaches",
      "bbox": [
